slowapi==0.1.9
# Batch 44. The API's only image decoder, and the reason profile pictures can be
# enabled at all: a magic-byte prefix proves a header, and re-encoding through a real
# imaging library is what neutralises the payload behind it. Kept on the newest patched
# line deliberately — this is the one dependency here whose whole job is parsing bytes
# a stranger chose.
pillow==12.3.0

# An unpinned transitive of pywebpush, and the one dependency that cannot be a single
# version everywhere. It publishes no Intel-macOS wheel above 46.0.3, and building it
# from source needs a Rust toolchain — which is why `scripts/ci-local.sh` had to force
# `--only-binary` for it.
#
# 46.0.3 is the newest release carrying both a manylinux x86_64 and a macOS x86_64
# wheel, so one lock installs identically in production and on the gate — which is the
# whole point of pinning, and it removes the `--only-binary` workaround ci-local.sh
# carried.
#
# A platform-split marker was tried first and rejected: `--universal` collapses it back
# to a single version anyway, so the marker read as doing something it did not.
#
# **This does pin behind the newest available (50.x).** Accepted here because nothing in
# this application calls cryptography directly — it is pywebpush's VAPID signing, using
# our own key, with no untrusted input parsed. If that stops being true, or a CVE lands
# in the gap, raise this bound and let the gate rebuild on a machine that has a wheel.
cryptography<=46.0.3
